Recommends: homelab-api, homelab-agent
Description: Indexed search over the fleet's mail and drive content
 Builds and maintains a normalized full-text index of every account's mail
 and drive files in Postgres, so search.mailmasker.org can answer a query
 without walking NFS. The two stores are mounted READ-ONLY and are read by
 the indexer only; the request path touches nothing but Postgres.
 .
 The schema is normalized past third normal form -- mime types, email
 addresses, the display names each address is seen under, per-message
 participant roles and an allowlist of headers all have their own
 relations, so a query can find a person rather than string-matching a
 header. Message body text and drive text are searchable through Postgres
 full-text vectors with weighted ranking.
 .
 No account can ever see another's data, and that is enforced by the
 database rather than by query discipline: every child row carries its
 account and references its parent by (parent, account) composite foreign
 key, so a cross-account write is a constraint violation; and row-level
 security with FORCE means a query that forgets its filter returns nothing
 instead of everything.
 .
 The indexer runs continuously on each of three hosts. Discovery is
 single-flight under a Postgres advisory lock; execution is shared from one
 queue via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, so the hosts balance themselves with no
 static partitioning and a dead host's work returns to the pool.
